First we note that by Lemma \ref{lmm:Divisor} the set of $m$ with $|\alpha_m|\ge(\log{x})^C$ has size $\ll x(\log{x})^{O_{B_0}(1)-C}$, so by Lemma \ref{lmm:SmallSets} these terms contribute negligibly if $C=C(A,B_0)$ is large enough. Thus, by dividing through by $(\log{x})^{C}$ and considering $A+C$ in place of $A$, it suffices to show the result when $|\alpha_m|\le 1$.

Since $N_1N_2N_3M\asymp x$ and $N_3\ge N_2\ge N_1$ we have
\[
